  "title": "Iqa‘ Ciftetelli 8/4",
  "subtitle": "(can also be played in 4/4)",
  "description": "Iqa‘ Ciftetelli",
  "lang": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Ciftetelli (pronounced \"shaftatalli\" in Arabic) is a Turkish usul that became popular in Arabic music. It is rarely used for composed melodies; instead, its primary use is to support improvisations (both vocal and instrumental).",
    "Ciftetelli is usually slow paced and stretched out over two 4/4 measures (see notation), and can share the same tempo and pace as Masmudi Kabir. Alternatively, it can be performed faster and lighter, in which case it can be notated in 4/4 and becomes very similar to Wahda w-Nuss (plus or minus some ornamentation)."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Ciftetelli 8/4 (can also be played in 4/4) Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Ciftetelli Iqa‘ Ciftetelli (pronounced \"shaftatalli\" in Arabic) is a Turkish usul that became popular in Arabic music. It is rarely used for composed melodies; instead, its primary use is to support improvisations (both vocal and instrumental). Ciftetelli is usually slow paced and stretched out over two 4/4 measures (see notation), and can share the same tempo and pace as Masmudi Kabir . Alternatively, it can be performed faster and lighter, in which case it can be notated in 4/4 and becomes very similar to Wahda w-Nuss (plus or minus some ornamentation). Ishta'tillak (1962) Vocals and Music by Farid al-Atrash Qasida Ja'at Mu‘adhibati Fatima Serhan The Queen of Balady Layali Rast (from ‘Addini ya M‘addawi) ‘Abbas al-Bleidi Mawwal Khullin Sagani Kasat al-Sabr Muhammad Khayri Ya Dala‘ Dalla‘ (1974) Sabah Music by Farid al-Atrash Qasida ‘Ayni Li Ghayri Jamalikum Al-Turath Ensemble Iqa‘ Ciftetelli 8/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan Examples of the faster form of Iqa‘ Ciftetelli that can be notated in 4/4 Bint el-Balad (1951) Instrumental Composition Muhammad Abdel Wahab Mawwal Ya Man Bunudak Harir Muhammad Khayri Nura Nura (1953) Vocals and Music by Farid al-Atrash Taqsim Nay Bayati Muhammad Khayri Tuta (1942) Instrumental Composition (from the movie Ahlam el-Shabab ) Music by Farid al-Atrash Ya Dara Duri Fina Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe",
